spi: rockchip: TX DMA burst length as a parameter

The driver hands the DMA controller a quarter of the FIFO (16 words) per
burst. On the RK3506 a burst holds the low-speed peripheral bus for its whole
length, and the Cortex-M0's GPIO writes (PicoCalc M0 audio: one per output
bit) wait behind it: measured, up to 72 core cycles (0.38 us) with 16-word
bursts and 16 with one-word bursts. See luckfox-lyra/docs/m0-audio.md in
picocalc-drivers. tx_burst=4 is the value to use with the display at
93.75 MHz: the frame rate stays at 48 a second and the M0's corrected audio
loop keeps pace. Shorter bursts cannot keep the FIFO full (24 frames a second
at tx_burst=1) and are worse for the M0 as well.

Tested as an out-of-tree copy of the driver bound to the display's
controller; this is the only functional change in it.

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-rockchip.c
@@
 #define DRIVER_NAME "rockchip-spi"

+/* Beats per TX DMA burst (0: a quarter of the FIFO) */
+static unsigned int tx_burst;
+module_param(tx_burst, uint, 0644);
+
@@ static int rockchip_spi_prepare_dma(struct rockchip_spi *rs,
 			.direction = DMA_MEM_TO_DEV,
 			.dst_addr = rs->dma_addr_tx,
 			.dst_addr_width = rs->n_bytes,
-			.dst_maxburst = rs->fifo_len / 4,
+			.dst_maxburst = tx_burst ? tx_burst : rs->fifo_len / 4,
 		};
